      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A typical residential roof replacement in Utah takes 1 to 3 days of active labor for standard asphalt shingles. Straightforward single-story homes can be finished in a single day, while larger properties, steep pitches, or complex multi-level layouts often require 2 to 5 days\n\n.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "1 to 3 days"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Factors Impacting the Timeline"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Size and Pitch: Larger square footage and steep angles require extra safety precautions and slower, more precise installation."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Material Type: Standard asphalt shingles go up fastest (1\u20132 days), while standing seam metal, tile, or specialized synthetic materials can take 3 to 5 days or longer.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Hidden Decking Damage: Rotted or water-damaged plywood underneath the shingles\u2014common with Utah's heavy winter snow loads\u2014adds repair time during tear-off.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Weather Delays: Sudden mountain rain, high winds, or heavy snow will pause work until conditions dry out safely."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          7
        ]
      },
      {
